<title>USA: NY to use tobacco settlement for health care.</title>
<headline>NY to use tobacco settlement for health care.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dennis Vacco, the New York State Attorney General, Friday said that the state expected to fund a new health care plan with part of the money it would get from an unprecedented settlement with the tobacco industry.</p>
<p>Vacco, in a prepared statement, said the settlement, announced in Washington between states and cigarette-makers, would give New York State $400 million in the first year, growing to $700 million by the fourth year.</p>
</text>
